## Nav2 navigation bridge: 2D mobile-robot path planning and path following as a service.
##
## This service runs a complete navigation stack (global planner, local controller,
## costmaps, recovery behaviors) but NEVER moves a robot by itself. The client owns the
## robot: it streams the robot's odometry, laser scans and a map IN, and reads velocity
## commands (cmd_vel) and plans OUT. The client decides whether and how to forward
## cmd_vel to its motors.
##
## Conventions (apply to every member unless stated otherwise):
##   * Units: meters, radians, seconds, m/s, rad/s. Angles are yaw about +Z, counter-
##     clockwise positive, range (-pi, pi].
##   * Robot body frame: +X forward, +Y left, +Z up (REP-103).
##   * Frames: "map" is the fixed world frame of the map supplied with map.load_map().
##     "odom" is the client's continuous odometry frame. Goals, plans and robot_pose are
##     in "map". Odometry is in "odom". Velocities are in the robot body frame.
##   * Pose2D = (orientation = yaw in rad, position = (x, y) in m).
##   * SpatialVelocity: only linear.x (forward m/s), linear.y (left m/s, holonomic only)
##     and angular.z (yaw rate rad/s) are used; all other components must be 0.
##   * All timestamps produced by the service are UNIX time in seconds (float) taken from
##     the service's clock. Data sent in is stamped with the service clock on arrival,
##     so client/service clock skew does not matter.
##
## Expected call order:
##   0. documentation("") returns this text; documentation("<member>") one entry.
##   1. configuration: set robot_radius/footprint, velocity limits, localization_mode
##      (only allowed while the stack is inactive).
##   2. map.load_map(grid).
##   3. Start streaming odometry (wire, >= 10 Hz) and laser_scan_in (pipe, >= 5 Hz).
##      In localization_mode external, also stream external_pose; in amcl mode call
##      initialize_localization() once.
##   4. start()  -> activates the stack; fails with a clear message if a precondition is
##      missing.
##   5. navigate_to_pose(goal) (or another generator); call Next() repeatedly to follow
##      progress. Meanwhile read cmd_vel and send it to the robot.
##   6. pause() / reset() / cancel_all() as needed.
##
## Choosing a member for an intent:
##   * "Plan only, do not move":            compute_path_to_pose / compute_path_through_poses
##   * "Go to a place":                     navigate_to_pose
##   * "Go via these places, in order":     navigate_through_poses (one continuous plan)
##   * "Visit each place and stop at each": follow_waypoints
##   * "Follow this exact path":            follow_path
##   * "Turn in place / back up / drive straight / pause": spin / backup / drive_on_heading / wait
##   * "Stop now":                          cancel_all (then read cmd_vel: it becomes zero)
##
## Safety: if odometry or laser input goes stale (see configuration.odometry_timeout /
## sensor_timeout) every active task is aborted, cmd_vel is forced to zero and
## nav_status.message explains why. Clients must also stop the robot themselves if
## cmd_vel.stamp stops advancing.
service experimental.nav2_bridge

stdver 0.10

import com.robotraconteur.geometry
import com.robotraconteur.laserscan
import com.robotraconteur.pointcloud
import com.robotraconteur.action

using com.robotraconteur.geometry.Point2D
using com.robotraconteur.geometry.Pose2D
using com.robotraconteur.geometry.SpatialVelocity
using com.robotraconteur.laserscan.LaserScan
using com.robotraconteur.pointcloud.PointCloudf
using com.robotraconteur.action.ActionStatusCode

## Lifecycle state of the navigation stack.
enum NavStackState
    ## Not started (initial state, and after reset()). Configuration may be changed.
    inactive = 0,
    ## start() is in progress.
    activating = 1,
    ## Ready: navigation and planning calls are accepted.
    active = 2,
    ## pause() was called: tasks are rejected, configuration still locked; call start() to resume.
    paused = 3,
    ## Activation or runtime failure. See NavStatus.message. Call reset() then start().
    error = 4
end

## How the robot's pose in the map frame is determined.
enum LocalizationMode
    ## The client streams the robot pose in the map frame on the external_pose wire
    ## (e.g. from its own SLAM, motion capture or simulation). Default.
    external = 0,
    ## The service runs AMCL particle-filter localization against the map using
    ## laser_scan_in. Call initialize_localization() before start() (and again any time
    ## to re-localize).
    amcl = 1
end

## Local controller (path-following algorithm).
enum ControllerType
    ## Model Predictive Path Integral controller. Smooth, robust; more CPU. Default.
    mppi = 0,
    ## Dynamic Window Approach controller. Lighter, more conservative.
    dwb = 1
end

## Odometry sample from the client's robot (pose and velocity in the "odom" frame).
struct Odometry2D
    ## Robot pose (base frame) in the client's odom frame. Must be continuous (no jumps).
    field Pose2D pose
    ## Robot body-frame velocity: linear.x, linear.y (holonomic only), angular.z.
    field SpatialVelocity velocity
    ## Monotonic sequence number chosen by the client. Optional (0 if unused).
    field uint64 seqno
end

## Velocity command produced by the navigation stack for the robot.
struct CmdVel
    ## Body-frame velocity to apply: linear.x (m/s), linear.y (m/s, holonomic only),
    ## angular.z (rad/s). All zero when no task is active.
    field SpatialVelocity velocity
    ## Service time (UNIX seconds) when this command was produced. If it stops
    ## advancing for more than ~0.5 s the client should stop the robot.
    field double stamp
    ## True while a task is actively commanding motion; false means "hold still".
    field bool active
    ## Increments with every new command.
    field uint64 seqno
end

## A path: ordered poses in the "map" frame.
struct Path2D
    ## Poses from start to goal; consecutive poses are typically 0.05 m apart.
    field Pose2D[] poses
    ## Service time (UNIX seconds) when the path was produced.
    field double stamp
    ## Total length along the path in meters.
    field double length
end

## Occupancy grid map supplied by the client.
struct OccupancyGrid
    ## Cell edge length in meters (e.g. 0.05). Must be > 0.
    field double resolution
    ## Number of cells along map X.
    field uint32 width
    ## Number of cells along map Y.
    field uint32 height
    ## Pose of the outer corner of cell (0,0) in the map frame. Usually orientation 0.
    field Pose2D origin
    ## width*height cells, row-major, row 0 at the origin: index = y*width + x.
    ## Values: 0 = free, 100 = occupied, 1..99 = probability (>= 65 treated as occupied),
    ## -1 = unknown.
    field int8[] data
end

## Metadata of a map or costmap whose cells are exposed through a memory member.
struct GridInfo
    ## Cell edge length in meters.
    field double resolution
    ## Number of cells along X.
    field uint32 width
    ## Number of cells along Y.
    field uint32 height
    ## Pose of the outer corner of cell (0,0) in the map frame (for the local costmap
    ## this moves with the robot).
    field Pose2D origin
    ## Service time (UNIX seconds) of the last update.
    field double stamp
    ## Increments every time the cells or metadata change. 0 = no data yet.
    field uint32 version
end

## Snapshot of the whole service state.
struct NavStatus
    ## Lifecycle state of the stack.
    field NavStackState stack_state
    ## Name of the running task ("navigate_to_pose", "spin", ...) or "" if idle.
    field string active_task
    ## Status of the running or most recently finished task.
    field ActionStatusCode task_status
    ## Robot pose in the map frame (valid only if localized is true).
    field Pose2D robot_pose
    ## True if a map->robot pose is currently known.
    field bool localized
    ## Remaining distance (m) of the current navigation task, or 0.
    field double distance_remaining
    ## Estimated remaining time (s) of the current navigation task, or 0.
    field double estimated_time_remaining
    ## True if odometry arrived within configuration.odometry_timeout.
    field bool odometry_ok
    ## True if laser scans (or point clouds) arrived within configuration.sensor_timeout.
    field bool sensors_ok
    ## True once map.load_map() succeeded.
    field bool map_ok
    ## Human-readable explanation of the current state, last error or watchdog trip.
    field string message
    ## Service time (UNIX seconds) of this status.
    field double stamp
end

## Progress of a navigation task (navigate_*, follow_waypoints, follow_path), returned by
## each Next() of the generator.
struct NavigationFeedback
    ## running while in progress; complete on the final item (then the generator ends).
    ## Failures are NOT reported here: Next() raises an exception instead.
    field ActionStatusCode status
    ## Robot pose in the map frame at the time of this feedback.
    field Pose2D current_pose
    ## Remaining distance in meters (navigate_*: to final goal; follow_path: to path end;
    ## 0 if not reported by the task).
    field double distance_remaining
    ## Seconds since the task started.
    field double navigation_time
    ## Estimated seconds to completion (0 if unknown).
    field double estimated_time_remaining
    ## Number of recovery behaviors run so far (navigate_* only).
    field int32 number_of_recoveries
    ## navigate_through_poses: poses remaining; follow_waypoints: index of the waypoint
    ## currently being approached (0-based); otherwise 0.
    field int32 waypoint_index
    ## follow_path only: current forward speed (m/s); otherwise 0.
    field double speed
    ## follow_waypoints final item only: indices of waypoints that could not be reached.
    field int32[] missed_waypoints
end

## Progress of a simple behavior (spin, backup, drive_on_heading, wait).
struct BehaviorFeedback
    ## running while in progress; complete on the final item.
    field ActionStatusCode status
    ## spin: radians turned so far (absolute); backup/drive_on_heading: meters traveled;
    ## wait: seconds remaining.
    field double progress
    ## Seconds since the behavior started.
    field double elapsed_time
end

## Root object. Connect with rr+tcp://<host>:62354?service=nav2
object Nav2Navigator

    ## START HERE. Returns documentation as text. name = "" returns the complete service
    ## definition with all usage notes (units, frames, call order, errors). name = a
    ## member ("navigate_to_pose"), a qualified member ("map.load_map",
    ## "configuration.robot_radius") or a type ("NavStatus") returns just that entry.
    ## Exists because Robot Raconteur does not transmit definition comments to clients.
    function string documentation(string name)

    ## INPUT. Stream the robot's odometry here continuously (>= 10 Hz recommended).
    ## Pose is in the client's odom frame and must not jump. Required before start().
    ## Rejected (ignored with nav_status.message set) if any value is NaN/Inf.
    wire Odometry2D odometry [writeonly]

    ## INPUT. Send every 2D laser scan here (>= 5 Hz recommended). Ranges in meters;
    ## scan_info.angle_min/angle_increment in radians relative to the sensor's +X axis.
    ## The sensor's mounting pose on the robot is configuration.laser_mount.
    ## Out-of-range readings may be +Inf or > range_max (treated as free space up to
    ## range_max). At most 10000 ranges per scan. Required before start().
    pipe LaserScan laser_scan_in [writeonly]

    ## INPUT (optional). 3D obstacle points already transformed into the robot body
    ## frame (+X forward, +Z up, origin on the floor below the robot center).
    ## Points between 0.05 m and 2.0 m height are marked as obstacles.
    ## At most 200000 points per message.
    pipe PointCloudf point_cloud_in [writeonly]

    ## INPUT (localization_mode external only). The robot's pose in the map frame,
    ## streamed continuously (>= 5 Hz). Ignored in amcl mode.
    wire Pose2D external_pose [writeonly]

    ## OUTPUT. The velocity command to send to the robot, updated at the controller rate
    ## (~20 Hz) while a task runs and set to zero (active=false) when idle, cancelled,
    ## failed or tripped by the watchdog. This is the final command after velocity
    ## smoothing and collision checking. Never apply a value whose stamp is older than
    ## ~0.5 s.
    wire CmdVel cmd_vel [readonly]

    ## OUTPUT. Latest global plan (map frame) of the running task, or from the most recent
    ## compute_path_* call. Empty poses if none.
    wire Path2D global_plan [readonly]

    ## OUTPUT. Short-horizon trajectory the local controller is currently following
    ## (map frame). Empty when idle.
    wire Path2D local_plan [readonly]

    ## OUTPUT. Robot pose in the map frame as used by the stack (~20 Hz). Check
    ## nav_status.localized before trusting it.
    wire Pose2D robot_pose [readonly]

    ## OUTPUT. Overall service state (~5 Hz). Read this first when something fails.
    wire NavStatus nav_status [readonly]

    ## Navigate to a goal pose in the map frame, planning around obstacles and running
    ## recovery behaviors when stuck. Returns a generator: call Next() repeatedly
    ## (each call blocks up to ~1 s and returns the latest NavigationFeedback). The last
    ## item has status complete; then Next() raises StopIteration.
    ## Errors: Next() raises OperationFailedException with the Nav2 error name and message
    ## (e.g. goal occupied, no valid path, timeout). Abort() or Close() cancels the goal and
    ## stops the robot (cmd_vel goes to zero). Starting a new navigation task preempts any
    ## running one (the old generator then raises OperationAbortedException).
    ## Precondition: stack_state active and robot localized.
    function NavigationFeedback{generator} navigate_to_pose(Pose2D goal)

    ## Navigate through several poses in order with one continuous plan, without stopping
    ## at intermediate poses. Orientation of intermediate poses is mostly ignored.
    ## 1..100 poses. Same generator semantics as navigate_to_pose.
    function NavigationFeedback{generator} navigate_through_poses(Pose2D[] poses)

    ## Visit each waypoint in order, navigating to each one as a separate goal (the robot
    ## stops at each). Waypoints that cannot be reached are skipped and listed in the final
    ## item's missed_waypoints. 1..100 waypoints. Same generator semantics.
    function NavigationFeedback{generator} follow_waypoints(Pose2D[] waypoints)

    ## Follow the given path (map frame) with the local controller, without global
    ## re-planning. Use a path from compute_path_* or one the client built (poses spaced
    ## <= 0.1 m). Obstacles on the path cause failure rather than detours.
    ## Same generator semantics.
    function NavigationFeedback{generator} follow_path(Path2D path)

    ## Rotate in place by target_yaw radians (positive = counter-clockwise; |value| <=
    ## 2*pi*3) within time_allowance seconds (> 0). Checks for collisions while turning.
    function BehaviorFeedback{generator} spin(double target_yaw, double time_allowance)

    ## Drive straight backwards distance meters (> 0) at speed m/s (> 0, the value is a
    ## magnitude) within time_allowance seconds. Stops early if a collision is predicted.
    function BehaviorFeedback{generator} backup(double distance, double speed, double time_allowance)

    ## Drive straight forward distance meters (> 0) at speed m/s (> 0) along the current
    ## heading within time_allowance seconds. Stops early if a collision is predicted.
    function BehaviorFeedback{generator} drive_on_heading(double distance, double speed, double time_allowance)

    ## Hold still (cmd_vel zero) for duration seconds (0 < duration <= 3600). Useful as a
    ## cancellable pause within a sequence.
    function BehaviorFeedback{generator} wait(double duration)

    ## PLANNING ONLY - never moves the robot. Compute a collision-free path from the
    ## robot's current pose to goal (map frame). Also published on global_plan.
    ## Errors: OperationFailedException with reason (start/goal occupied or outside the
    ## map, no valid path, timeout). Precondition: stack active and robot localized.
    function Path2D compute_path_to_pose(Pose2D goal)

    ## PLANNING ONLY. Like compute_path_to_pose but from an explicit start pose instead of
    ## the robot's current pose (does not require localization). Useful for "how far is
    ## A from B" questions.
    function Path2D compute_path_from_pose(Pose2D start, Pose2D goal)

    ## PLANNING ONLY. Compute one continuous path from the robot's current pose through
    ## all goals in order (1..100 goals).
    function Path2D compute_path_through_poses(Pose2D[] goals)

    ## Cancel every running task immediately; cmd_vel becomes zero. Safe to call at any
    ## time, including when idle. Running generators raise OperationAbortedException.
    function void cancel_all()

    ## Clear obstacles from both costmaps (e.g. after a door opened or a person moved).
    ## Obstacles still visible to the sensors reappear on the next scan.
    function void clear_costmaps()

    ## amcl mode only: tell AMCL roughly where the robot is in the map (position error
    ## < ~1 m, yaw error < ~0.5 rad). Required before start() in amcl mode; may be called
    ## again while active to re-localize. In external mode raises
    ## InvalidOperationException.
    function void initialize_localization(Pose2D pose)

    ## Activate the navigation stack with the current configuration. Blocks until active
    ## (typically 4-10 s, at most ~60 s; set the client request timeout to >= 60 s). Preconditions (InvalidOperationException listing what is
    ## missing): map set, odometry streaming, laser scans streaming, and in external mode
    ## external_pose streaming, in amcl mode initialize_localization() called. From
    ## paused, resumes. No-op when already active.
    function void start()

    ## Cancel running tasks and deactivate the stack (cmd_vel zero). Configuration stays
    ## locked. start() resumes quickly.
    function void pause()

    ## Cancel tasks and return the stack to inactive so configuration can be changed or
    ## an error cleared. Map and input streams are kept.
    function void reset()

    ## The map (static occupancy grid) used for planning and localization.
    objref OccupancyMap map

    ## Global costmap: the static map plus inflated obstacles, used by the planner.
    objref Costmap global_costmap

    ## Local costmap: rolling window around the robot from live sensor data, used by the
    ## controller.
    objref Costmap local_costmap

    ## Robot and algorithm parameters. Changes are only allowed while stack_state is
    ## inactive (call reset() first) and take effect on the next start().
    objref NavConfiguration configuration
end

## The static map of the environment, supplied by the client.
object OccupancyMap

    ## Replace the map. Allowed in any state; while active, the planner and costmaps
    ## switch to the new map within ~1 s (running tasks continue and re-plan).
    ## Limits: resolution 0.01..1.0 m, width*height <= 10,000,000 cells, data length must
    ## equal width*height. Raises InvalidArgumentException on bad input.
    function void load_map(OccupancyGrid map)

    ## Return the current map. Raises InvalidOperationException if no map was set.
    function OccupancyGrid read_map()

    ## Metadata of the current map (version 0 = no map yet).
    property GridInfo info [readonly]

    ## Map cells (same encoding as OccupancyGrid.data), for partial reads of large maps.
    ## Length width*height (0 if no map).
    memory int8[] data [readonly]

    ## Fired after the map changes; the argument is the new info.version.
    event map_changed(uint32 version)
end

## A costmap maintained by the navigation stack. Cell values are uint8 costs:
## 0 = free, 1..252 = increasing cost near obstacles (inflation), 253 = inscribed (robot
## center here would collide), 254 = lethal obstacle, 255 = unknown.
object Costmap

    ## Metadata of the latest costmap (version 0 = not available yet, e.g. stack inactive).
    property GridInfo info [readonly]

    ## Latest costmap cells, row-major (index = y*width + x). Length width*height.
    memory uint8[] data [readonly]

    ## Clear this costmap's obstacle layers.
    function void clear()

    ## Cost (0..255) of the cell containing the map-frame point (x, y); 255 if outside.
    function uint8 cost_at(double x, double y)
end

## Robot geometry, limits and algorithm options. Properties are readable at any time but
## writable only while the stack is inactive; writing otherwise raises
## InvalidOperationException. Out-of-range values raise InvalidArgumentException.
object NavConfiguration

    ## Circular robot radius in meters (0.05..3.0). Used when footprint is empty.
    ## Default 0.22.
    property double robot_radius

    ## Polygonal footprint in the robot body frame (3..64 points, meters, counter-
    ## clockwise). Empty list = use robot_radius. Default empty.
    property Point2D[] footprint

    ## Maximum forward speed m/s (0.01..5.0). Default 0.5.
    property double max_linear_velocity

    ## Maximum reverse speed m/s as a magnitude (0..5.0); 0 forbids driving backwards
    ## during navigation (backup still works). Default 0.0.
    property double max_reverse_velocity

    ## Maximum yaw rate rad/s (0.05..10.0). Default 1.5.
    property double max_angular_velocity

    ## Maximum linear acceleration m/s^2 (0.05..10.0). Default 1.0.
    property double max_linear_acceleration

    ## Maximum angular acceleration rad/s^2 (0.05..20.0). Default 3.0.
    property double max_angular_acceleration

    ## True for omnidirectional robots (uses linear.y). Default false (differential drive).
    property bool holonomic

    ## Local controller algorithm. Default mppi.
    property ControllerType controller

    ## How map localization is obtained. Default external.
    property LocalizationMode localization_mode

    ## Laser sensor mounting pose in the robot body frame (yaw rad, x/y m). Default 0.
    property Pose2D laser_mount

    ## Extra clearance kept from obstacles in meters, beyond the robot footprint
    ## (0..5.0). Default 0.35.
    property double inflation_radius

    ## Goal reached when within this distance in meters (0.01..2.0). Default 0.25.
    property double goal_xy_tolerance

    ## Goal reached when within this yaw error in radians (0.01..3.15). Default 0.25.
    property double goal_yaw_tolerance

    ## Watchdog: odometry older than this many seconds aborts tasks (0.1..5.0).
    ## Default 0.5.
    property double odometry_timeout

    ## Watchdog: laser/point-cloud data older than this many seconds aborts tasks
    ## (0.1..5.0). Default 1.0.
    property double sensor_timeout

    ## Restore every property to its default. Same state restriction as writes.
    function void reset_to_defaults()

    ## All properties as a name -> value map (for logging or display).
    function varvalue{string} describe()
end
